+---
+id: task-001-rental-module-basics
+type: task
+title: "Rental module basics"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Rental module basics
+
+Request: give the booking desk a rental module, in memory, covering the basics: equipment, quotes,
+and bookings for boards and sails.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Export `createRentalService()` from `src/index.ts`. It returns a service with:
+  - `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`: `id` is a string, `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`,
+    `dailyPrice` is the price of one rental day in euro cents.
+  - `quote({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`.
+  - `book({ itemId, start, end })`: books the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+- `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period the rules do not allow.
+- `book` also throws when the item is not free for the whole period.
+- Cancellation is out of scope; the policy is recorded here for later.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- A quote for an item over `n` whole days is `n * dailyPrice`, an integer number of euro cents.
+- Times are full ISO-8601 UTC timestamps ending in `Z`. Date-only or offset-based strings are rejected.
+- A period starts at midnight UTC and ends at midnight UTC, and it ends after it starts. Otherwise it is rejected.
+- Periods are half-open: `[start, end)`. A booking ending at midnight does not overlap one starting then.
+- The same item cannot hold two bookings whose periods overlap.
+- Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, `booking-2`, ...), so results are deterministic.
+- `addEquipment` rejects an unknown `kind`, a negative or non-integer `dailyPrice`, and a duplicate `id`.
+
+## Rules applied
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+2. Times are in UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days only.
+4. The same item cannot be booked twice for overlapping periods.
+5. Cancellation policy (not implemented yet): a booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start
+   gets no refund; otherwise the full amount is refunded.
+
+## Traceability
+
+No requirement documents exist yet for this module. This task is the first link of the chain for it:
+request -> this task -> acceptance above -> tests in `test/`.
